<h3>1.7 Design alternatives — evidenced?</h3>
<p>Three complete programs, each passing the same check driver (<code>checks/check_run_v{1,2,3}_output.txt</code>, re-run here). v1→v2 (arrays+indices → <code>Vec</code>/<code>Mat</code>) rests on the reproduced gaps #4/#5 and on the <code>Indexed⟦Value,ℤ32⟧</code>/<code>Array2⟦…⟧</code> signature noise visible in <code>figures/v1_layer.svg</code>. v2→v3 (KV cache → whole sequence): pure function of the token list, positions as comprehension iterations, paper-shaped Q/K/V, one-call loss — all visible in the source; "may run in parallel" is by semantics, unmeasured, and marked so; the smoke-forward timings 2.0 / 3.3 / 4.1 s are in <code>transcript.txt</code>. Autograd shapes (pairs vs lists vs closures) all run with figures. The unified Σ over an <code>Additive</code> trait runs but has static type <code>Additive</code> and was declined — the one place a nicer notation was refused for typing honesty. Not explored: a matrix–matrix product (so <code>Q = X W_qᵀ</code> stays a comprehension); the spec's postfix <code>^T</code>.</p>

